# Purpose
Explains safe handling of CSV files, including opening, editing, dates, numbers,
and column-shape checks.

# Key Sections
- When to use CSV.
- Before opening a CSV.
- Opening CSV files.
- Editing CSV files.
- Dates and numbers.
- Missing or extra columns.

# Dependencies
- Belongs to the productivity manual set.

# Gotchas
- CSV edits can silently change dates, leading zeros, encodings, and delimiter
  assumptions. Tell users to preserve originals before risky changes.

